# The built-in `fetch-url` policy: what a fresh install allows before any
# IT department has written its own `/etc/exarch/fetch-policy.ral`.  Small
# and conservative on purpose — widen it by installing a real policy file,
# never by editing this one.
#
# `allow` entries are either an exact hostname or a `*.suffix` wildcard.
# `max-bytes` caps one response body; `rate-per-minute` caps how many
# fetches this process (and everything it spawns) may make per minute.

return [
  allow: ['*.bristol.ac.uk'],
  max-bytes: 2097152,
  rate-per-minute: 10,
]
